    {
      "id": "cicd.pipeline",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "workflows",
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "dev is the sole development branch and main is read-only. Do not create other development branches, force-push, rebase shared history, or bypass gates. Automatic promotion is currently absent; main must not advance until dev deployment smoke tests, image signing, and compare-and-swap gates are restored. Future release automation may only fast-forward main and then create a version tag and GitHub Release for the same SHA, stopping on divergence or ref movement. Commit, push, and GitHub actions require explicit task authorization."
    },
    {
      "id": "constraints.project",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "constraints",
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Preserve service ownership and explicit dependency injection; prohibit global mutable configuration or clients, service locators, unowned goroutines, unbounded retries, panic or os.Exit outside process entrypoints, and internal error leakage. scripts/generated-files.txt is the sole generated-ownership manifest; never hand-edit listed files, kitex_gen, or services/collaboration/src/generated. IDL sources are under idl/http/v1 and idl/rpc/v1 and generation must use repository scripts. Resource creation, readiness, shutdown, and cleanup follow bounded, reverse-order lifecycle rules. Documentation must describe only implemented and verified behavior and be updated when public runtime, contracts, boundaries, lifecycle, startup, or APIs change."
    },
    {
      "id": "conventions.code-style",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "conventions",
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Go constructors validate required dependencies and return (T, error); errors add operation context, preserve causes with %w, and use errors.Is/As. Context, deadlines, request IDs, and traces propagate end to end. Use pkg/codec/json for strict HTTP JSON and reuse shared auth, error, log, metadata, trace, and metrics contracts. Rust must pass rustfmt, clippy -D warnings, and cargo deny. Tests stay near implementations and cover success, boundaries, dependency failures, error mapping, cleanup/rollback, and concurrency with deterministic synchronization. Repository text uses LF except .bat and .cmd."
    },
    {
      "id": "entrypoints.catalog",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "services",
      "sources": [
        {
          "detail": "evidence-sha256:0f227a4dc8cecdf021566a02b5ca6fbbf05b21bec287a80f8b951c3f74d51096",
          "kind": "detected",
          "reference": "filesystem:entrypoint-candidates"
        },
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Service process entrypoints are services/gateway/main.go, services/identity/main.go, services/knowledge/main.go, and services/collaboration/src/main.rs. Service main files only create and execute application commands; Go spec files only declare application specifications. Supporting executable entrypoints include scripts/idlguard, collaboration Rust code generation, and tools/authkeys, tools/configctl, and tools/interop. Deployment definitions live under deploy and docker."
    },
    {
      "id": "environment.setup",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "environment",
      "sources": [
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Go module plus a Rust workspace under services/collaboration. Use repository-pinned generators (Kitex 0.16.2, hz 0.9.7 via hz update only, thriftgo 0.4.5) and rustc 1.97.1 from rust-toolchain.toml. The collaboration interop fixture requires Node.js >= 24.18.1 and npm ci. Inject all non-public configuration through environment variables or deployment-platform secret management; never store secret values in repository configuration."
    },
