        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Secrets are injected only through environment variables or deployment-platform secret managers. Never place passwords, DSNs, JWTs, private keys, authorization/cookies, or API keys in YAML, source, snapshots, logs, metric labels, or span attributes. Logs use pkg/log and slog with context and stable low-cardinality fields; metrics use bounded route/RPC/status/code/dependency labels. External request IDs and W3C trace context follow shared middleware rules, and authentication, identity recheck, trusted-proxy, and rate-limit decisions fail closed on dependency errors."
    },
    {
      "id": "services.catalog",
      "revision": 2,
      "section": "services",
      "sources": [
        {
          "detail": "evidence-sha256:4861a558e13e8261cad5522bcd050aeb7c528bee7c7ce522497d57fee6c27f8e",
          "kind": "detected",
          "reference": "filesystem:service-definitions"
        },
        {
          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-08T01:14:27Z",
      "value": "Gateway is the HTTP edge and calls typed upstream clients without accessing Identity storage. Identity owns identity domain behavior and persistence. Knowledge owns document metadata, permissions, publication/public projections, attachments, trash, quotas, and outbox in the PostgreSQL knowledge schema, but not Yjs binary state. Collaboration is the Rust Volo Thrift and WebSocket/Yrs service; it owns collaboration state in its PostgreSQL schema and rechecks document access through Knowledge RPC."
    },
